    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d148">

                <pb facs="0142" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.24/195: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-23T16:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>133. Your 147, May 10, last paragraph. Could not the Central Supply Committee
                    recommended in your 119, April 23<anchor n="15" xml:id="d148-f1"/> and
                    authorized <pb facs="0143" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/> by Department’s 106, April
                        30<anchor n="16" xml:id="d148-f2"/> act in a general supervisory capacity to
                    direct distribution of the tires in question as well as other commodities
                    furnished by the United States under Lend-Lease or otherwise? Would it be
                    practicable and advisable to consign such goods to the Iranian Government in
                    care of your Legation or the Central Supply Committee—distribution policies to
                    be decided upon by the Committee and actual distribution to be done by existing
                    UKCC or Iranian agencies under supervision of the Committee? It is Department’s
                    tentative thought that such an arrangement would have desirable effect of
                    integrating entire supply and distribution system.</p>
                <p>If you concur, please indicate what if any additional staff you would need to
                    participate fully in the work of the Committee on this basis.</p>
                <p>Please keep the Department informed of progress made in setting up Central Supply
                    Committee.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
